IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`
IMPORT `chapter-16-sexual-general`

§ `Chapter 16 -- Sexual offences: insult to modesty, voyeurism, images and abuse material`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 377BA, 377BB, 377BC, 377BD, 377BE, 377BF, 377BG, 377BH, 377BI,
-- 377BJ, 377BK, 377BL, 377BM, 377BN, 377BO.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Shape of the group. s 377BA is the old insult-to-modesty offence and stands alone.
-- ss 377BB to 377BF are a chain about images of adults and children alike: making
-- them (voyeurism, s 377BB), distributing them (s 377BC), possessing or producing
-- them (s 377BD), distributing or threatening to distribute intimate ones
-- (s 377BE), and exposure (s 377BF). ss 377BG to 377BL are the child abuse material
-- offences and their 16-to-18 counterpart in abusive material. ss 377BM and 377BN
-- are the defences, and s 377BO the extraterritorial extension.
--
-- The defences are the reason this module is worth reading carefully. ss 377BM and
-- 377BN are not general exceptions in the Chapter 4 sense: each names the exact
-- sections it answers, and they differ. s 377BM(1) answers only s 377BD; s 377BM(2)
-- answers ss 377BB, 377BC, 377BD and 377BE(1) -- note, not 377BE(2), the threat
-- limb. s 377BN(1) answers only s 377BK; s 377BN(2), (3) and (4) answer ss 377BH to
-- 377BK, which does NOT include s 377BG. Each is therefore conjoined only to the
-- sections it belongs to, and the encoding keeps them apart rather than gathering
-- them into one "a defence applies".
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. Almost every section here raises the maximum where the
-- person depicted is below 14. That fact is not carried as an element because it
-- changes no test in these sections; where a section makes an age an element -- as
-- ss 377BG and 377BL do -- it is carried.

§§ `Section 377BA -- Word or gesture intended to insult modesty`

-- Whoever, intending to insult the modesty of any person, utters a word, makes a
-- sound or gesture, or exhibits an object, intending that it be heard or seen by
-- that person, OR intrudes upon the privacy of that person.
--
-- The final limb is a true alternative to the intended-perception limb: the section
-- reads "..., or intrudes upon the privacy of such person", so an intrusion on
-- privacy with intent to insult modesty is within the section whether or not
-- anything was uttered for that person to hear.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BA"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a word or gesture intended to insult modesty under Penal Code 1871 section 377BA
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc An intent to insult modesty, with either a word, sound, gesture or object intended to be perceived by that person, or an intrusion upon that person's privacy.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes insulting the modesty of a person` IF
        i's `intending to insult the modesty of any person utters a word makes a sound or gesture or exhibits an object`
    AND (   i's `intending that such word or sound will be heard or that such gesture or object will be seen by that person`
         OR i's `intrudes upon the privacy of that person`)

§§ `Section 377BB -- Voyeurism`

-- Five offences in subsections (1) to (5), each with the same second paragraph --
-- that the accused knows or has reason to believe the other person does not consent.
-- Subsections (1) to (3) are about a private act: observing it, operating equipment
-- to enable its observation, or recording it. Subsections (4) and (5) are about the
-- genital region, breasts or buttocks in circumstances where they or the underwear
-- would not otherwise be visible: operating equipment to enable observation, or
-- recording an image.
-- s 377BB(6) is a sixth offence: installing equipment, or constructing or adapting a
-- structure, intending to enable any of the five. It stands on its own and does not
-- need the knowledge element, which is why it is disjoined outside the conjunction.
--
-- s 377BB(9) presumes, until the contrary is proved, that the person did not consent
-- where a recording was made. A rebuttable presumption of fact, not an element; not
-- encoded.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BB(1) to (5)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 377BB voyeurism limb is made out` IF
        i's `intentionally observes another person doing a private act without that person consent`
    OR  i's `operates equipment with the intention of enabling the accused or another to observe a third person doing a private act without that person consent`
    OR  i's `intentionally or knowingly records another person doing a private act without that person consent`
    OR  i's `operates equipment without another person consent with the intention of enabling the accused or another to observe that person genital region breasts if female or buttocks whether exposed or covered in circumstances where they or the underwear would not otherwise be visible`
    OR  i's `intentionally or knowingly records without another person consent an image of that person genital region breasts if female or buttocks whether exposed or covered in such circumstances`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BB"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes voyeurism under Penal Code 1871 section 377BB
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc One of the five voyeurism limbs together with knowledge or reason to believe there was no consent, or the s 377BB(6) offence of installing equipment or adapting a structure to enable one of them.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voyeurism` IF
        (    `a section 377BB voyeurism limb is made out` i
         AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the other person does not consent`)
    OR  i's `installs equipment or constructs or adapts a structure or part of a structure with the intention of enabling the accused or another to commit an offence under section 377BB(1) to (5)`

§§ `Section 377BC -- Distribution of a voyeuristic image or recording`

-- Distributing, or possessing for the purpose of distributing, an image or recording
-- of another person without that person's consent, knowing or having reason to
-- believe it was obtained through a s 377BB offence, and knowing or having reason to
-- believe that person does not consent to the distribution.
-- All three paragraphs are conjuncts in each subsection; the two subsections differ
-- only in distribution versus possession for distribution.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BC"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes distribution of a voyeuristic image or recording under Penal Code 1871 section 377BC
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc Distributing or possessing for distribution an image obtained through a s 377BB offence, without consent and with knowledge or reason to believe both of those things.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes distribution of a voyeuristic image` IF
        (   i's `intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of another person without that person consent to the distribution`
         OR i's `intentionally or knowingly has in his possession an image or recording of another person for the purpose of distribution without that person consent`)
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB`
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the other person does not consent to the distribution`

§§ `Section 377BD -- Possession or production of a voyeuristic or intimate image`

-- s 377BD(1) is possession of, or gained access to, an image of another person where
-- EITHER (a) the accused knows or has reason to believe it was obtained through a
-- s 377BB offence, OR (b) he knows or has reason to believe all three of: that it is
-- an intimate image or recording as defined in s 377BE(5); that the possession or
-- access was without the consent of the person depicted; and that it will or is
-- likely to cause that person humiliation, alarm or distress. Limb (b)'s three
-- sub-paragraphs are conjoined -- the section says "and" between them.
--
-- s 377BD(5) is a separate offence of intentionally producing an intimate image
-- without consent, knowing or having reason to believe it will or is likely to cause
-- humiliation, alarm or distress.
-- s 377BD(4) and (8) explain what possession, access and production include. They
-- widen what may be asserted and add no limb.
--
-- Both are answered by the s 377BM defences, which is why they are built separately
-- and the defences applied at the end.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BD(1)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 377BD(1) possession offence is made out` IF
        i's `has in his possession or has gained access to an image or recording of another person`
    AND (   i's `knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB`
         OR (    i's `knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording is an intimate image or recording`
              AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to it was without the consent of the person depicted`
              AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to it will or is likely to cause humiliation alarm or distress to the person depicted`))

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BD(5)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 377BD(5) production offence is made out` IF
        i's `intentionally produces an intimate image or recording of another person without that person consent`
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the production will or is likely to cause humiliation alarm or distress to that person`

§§ `Section 377BE -- Distributing or threatening to distribute an intimate image`

-- s 377BE(1): intentionally or knowingly distributing an intimate image of another
-- person, without that person's consent, knowing or having reason to believe it will
-- or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress.
-- s 377BE(2): knowingly threatening the distribution, on the same terms.
-- s 377BE(6): on the threat limb the prosecution need not prove that the image
-- exists, or that it is in fact an intimate image. That removes elements rather than
-- adding them, so the threat limb does not conjoin the existence of the image.
--
-- s 377BE(5) defines "intimate image or recording", including an altered or
-- generated image but excluding one so altered that no reasonable person would
-- believe it depicts the person. Illustrations (a) and (b) are the two sides of that
-- line -- a face pasted onto a real body is intimate, a face pasted onto a cartoon is
-- not. The definition is carried inside the intimate-image facts.
--
-- Only s 377BE(1) is answered by the s 377BM(2) defence; s 377BE(2) is not.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BE(1)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 377BE(1) distribution offence is made out` IF
        i's `intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of another person`
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the other person does not consent to the distribution`
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the distribution or threat will or is likely to cause that person humiliation alarm or distress`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BE(2)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes threatening to distribute an intimate image under Penal Code 1871 section 377BE(2)
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc A knowing threat to distribute an intimate image without consent, likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress. The image need not exist and need not in fact be intimate.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes threatening to distribute an intimate image` IF
        i's `knowingly threatens the distribution of an intimate image or recording of another person`
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the other person does not consent to the distribution`
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the distribution or threat will or is likely to cause that person humiliation alarm or distress`

§§ `Section 377BF -- Sexual exposure`

-- Exposing the accused's own genitals, or distributing an image of anyone's
-- genitals, in each case for sexual gratification or to cause humiliation, alarm or
-- distress, intending that the other person will see them, and without that
-- person's consent.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BF"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual exposure under Penal Code 1871 section 377BF
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc Exposing genitals or distributing an image of genitals, for sexual gratification or to cause distress, intending the other person to see them, without consent.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual exposure` IF
        (   i's `for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person humiliation alarm or distress intentionally exposes the accused genitals`
         OR i's `for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person humiliation alarm or distress intentionally distributes to that person an image of the accused or any other person genitals`)
    AND i's `intends that the other person will see those genitals`
    AND i's `does so without the other person consent`

§§ `Sections 377BG to 377BK -- Child abuse material`

-- Five offences, each conjoined with knowledge or reason to believe that the
-- material is child abuse material, and each requiring that the material in fact be
-- child abuse material as s 377C(1) defines it:
--   s 377BG  using, or causing or procuring or allowing the use of, a person below
--            16 in the production of such material
--   s 377BH  intentionally producing it
--   s 377BI  distributing, selling, offering for sale, or possessing for those
--   s 377BJ  advertising it, or announcing an offer to acquire or access it
--   s 377BK  possessing it or having gained access to it
--
-- s 377BG is the only one of the five with an age element of its own, and the only
-- one the s 377BN(2) to (4) defences do NOT answer -- those run to "sections 377BH to
-- 377BK". s 377BN(1) answers s 377BK alone.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BG"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes using or involving a child in the production of child abuse material under Penal Code 1871 section 377BG
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc Using, causing or procuring the use of, or (having care or custody) consenting to or allowing the use of, a person below 16 in producing material known or believed to be child abuse material.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes using a child in producing child abuse material` IF
        (   i's `uses a person below 16 years of age for the production of such material`
         OR i's `causes or procures a person of that age to be so used`
         OR i's `having the care or custody of a person of that age consents to the person being so used or allows the person to be so used`)
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BH, 377BI, 377BJ and 377BK"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 377BH to 377BK conduct limb is made out` IF
        i's `intentionally produces child abuse material`
    OR  i's `distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material or has it in possession for the purpose of such distribution sale or offer`
    OR  i's `for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale child abuse material advertises the material`
    OR  i's `announces or otherwise makes known by any means an offer or purported offer to acquire buy or gain access to child abuse material`
    OR  i's `has in possession or has gained access to child abuse material`

§§ `Section 377BL -- Exploitation by abusive material of a minor of or above 16 but below 18`

-- s 377BL(1) confines the section to a relationship exploitative of a person of or
-- above 16 but below 18. Subsections (2) to (4) then mirror ss 377BG, 377BH and
-- 377BI for "abusive material" of that person, which s 377BL(6) defines in the same
-- shape as child abuse material but keyed to that particular person.
-- This is a 16-to-18 offence, so s 377D(2) makes a reasonable mistaken belief that
-- the minor was 18 a defence, subject to the s 377D(3) defeaters.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BL"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes exploitation by abusive material of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 under Penal Code 1871 section 377BL
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc An exploitative relationship with a person of or above 16 but below 18, and the use, production or distribution of abusive material of that person.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The exploitative-relationship test of s 377CA, and the s 377D mistake-as-to-age defence which is available on this section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes exploitation by abusive material of a minor` i c IF
        i's `the accused is in a relationship with a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age that is exploitative of that person`
    AND `the relationship is exploitative of the minor` c
    AND i's `the material is abusive material of that person as defined in section 377BL(6)`
    AND (   i's `uses that person for the production of abusive material or causes or procures that person to be so used`
         OR i's `intentionally produces abusive material of that person`
         OR i's `distributes or sells or offers for sale abusive material of that person or has it in possession for the purpose of such distribution sale or offer`)
    AND (NOT `a mistake as to age is a defence` c)

§§ `Sections 377BM and 377BN -- The defences`

-- Two defences recur in both sections and are gathered here.
--
-- The INADVERTENT POSSESSION defence: the accused did not intentionally come into
-- possession or gain access, and on becoming aware took all reasonable steps as soon
-- as practicable to cease possession or access. s 377BM(1) gives it against s 377BD;
-- s 377BN(1) gives it against s 377BK. Both halves are required.
--
-- The LEGITIMATE PURPOSE defence: the act was done for the prevention, detection,
-- investigation or punishment of an offence, for proceedings or evidence, or for
-- safety or national security, without intent to cause injury to the person depicted
-- and with reasonable cause, AND the material was not kept longer than reasonably
-- necessary for that purpose. s 377BM(2) gives it against ss 377BB, 377BC, 377BD and
-- 377BE(1); s 377BN(2) against ss 377BH to 377BK. All three conjuncts are required --
-- the Illustrations to s 377BM(2) both turn on the purpose and on the material being
-- handed over rather than kept.
--
-- s 377BN(3) and (4) are specific to child abuse material: a legitimate purpose
-- related to science, medicine, education or art that posed no undue risk of harm to
-- a person below 16; and the accused being below 16 where the material is an image
-- of the accused alone.
-- s 377BN(5) provides that a mistaken belief that reasonable persons would not regard
-- the material as offensive is NOT a defence. It is encoded as nothing -- a fact
-- carried so a caller can assert it, contributing to no rule, which is the correct
-- encoding of a provision that closes a defence off.
-- s 377BN(6) gives a marriage defence to ss 377BG(1), 377BH(1), 377BI, 377BJ(2) and
-- 377BK(1) on detailed conditions about who is depicted and who consented. Those
-- conditions are not encoded: they turn on facts about the material's content that
-- this record does not carry, and the register records the gap.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BM(1) and 377BN(1)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inadvertent possession defence is made out` IF
        i's `did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to the image recording or material`
    AND i's `on becoming aware took all reasonable steps in the circumstances as soon as practicable to cease possession of or access to it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BM(2) and 377BN(2)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the legitimate purpose defence is made out` IF
        i's `the act was done for the prevention detection investigation or punishment of an offence for the conduct of proceedings or to obtain evidence or for safety or national security`
    AND i's `the act was done without intent to cause injury to the person depicted and with reasonable cause`
    AND i's `the image recording or material was not kept for longer than was reasonably necessary or required for that purpose`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BN(3) and (4)"
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 377BN(3) or (4) defence is made out` IF
        (    i's `the act has a legitimate purpose related to science medicine education or art`
         AND i's `the act did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age`)
    OR  i's `the accused is below 16 years of age and the child abuse material is an image of the accused alone`

§§ `The offences, with their own defences applied`

-- Each offence conjoins only the defences its own section names. s 377BD has both
-- s 377BM defences; ss 377BB, 377BC and 377BE(1) have only the legitimate-purpose
-- one; s 377BE(2) has neither; s 377BK has both s 377BN defences plus s 377BN(3) and
-- (4); ss 377BH to 377BJ have the s 377BN(2) to (4) defences but not s 377BN(1);
-- and s 377BG has none of them.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BB and 377BM(2)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes voyeurism under Penal Code 1871 section 377BB after its own defence
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc The voyeurism facts, and the s 377BM(2) legitimate-purpose defence which answers this section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voyeurism after defences` IF
        `constitutes voyeurism` i
    AND (NOT `the legitimate purpose defence is made out` i)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BC and 377BM(2)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes distribution of a voyeuristic image under Penal Code 1871 section 377BC after its own defence
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc The s 377BC facts, and the s 377BM(2) legitimate-purpose defence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes distribution of a voyeuristic image after defences` IF
        `constitutes distribution of a voyeuristic image` i
    AND (NOT `the legitimate purpose defence is made out` i)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BD, 377BM(1) and 377BM(2)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possession or production of a voyeuristic or intimate image under Penal Code 1871 section 377BD after its own defences
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc The s 377BD possession and production offences, with both s 377BM defences, which answer this section alone.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possession or production of an intimate image after defences` IF
        (   `the section 377BD(1) possession offence is made out` i
         OR `the section 377BD(5) production offence is made out` i)
    AND (NOT `the inadvertent possession defence is made out` i)
    AND (NOT `the legitimate purpose defence is made out` i)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BE(1) and 377BM(2)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes distributing an intimate image under Penal Code 1871 section 377BE(1) after its own defence
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc The s 377BE(1) distribution offence, with the s 377BM(2) defence. The threat limb in s 377BE(2) has no defence and is decided separately.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes distributing an intimate image after defences` IF
        `the section 377BE(1) distribution offence is made out` i
    AND (NOT `the legitimate purpose defence is made out` i)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 377BH, 377BI, 377BJ, 377BK and 377BN"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a child abuse material offence under Penal Code 1871 sections 377BH to 377BK after their defences
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc Producing, distributing, advertising or possessing child abuse material, with the s 377BN defences. s 377BN(1) answers only the possession limb.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a child abuse material offence after defences` IF
        `a section 377BH to 377BK conduct limb is made out` i
    AND i's `knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`
    AND (NOT `the legitimate purpose defence is made out` i)
    AND (NOT `a section 377BN(3) or (4) defence is made out` i)
    AND (NOT (    i's `has in possession or has gained access to child abuse material`
              AND `the inadvertent possession defence is made out` i))

§§ `Section 377BO -- Child abuse material offences outside or partially outside Singapore`

-- A citizen or permanent resident who does outside Singapore any act that would, if
-- done here, be an offence under s 377BG, s 377BH or s 377BL(2) or (3), is guilty of
-- that offence. Note the section deems the offence to be the underlying one rather
-- than creating a separate one.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377BO(1)"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 377BO reaches a child abuse material offence committed outside Singapore
GIVEN i IS A `Sexual Image` @desc A citizen or permanent resident doing outside Singapore an act that would be an offence under s 377BG, s 377BH or s 377BL(2) or (3) if done here.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 377BO reaches the act committed outside Singapore` IF
        i's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND i's `does outside Singapore an act that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BG 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes insulting the modesty of a person` IF
        `constitutes insulting the modesty of a person` (a's `sexual image`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes voyeurism` IF
        `constitutes voyeurism after defences` (a's `sexual image`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an intimate image offence` IF
        (   `constitutes distribution of a voyeuristic image after defences` (a's `sexual image`)
         OR `constitutes possession or production of an intimate image after defences` (a's `sexual image`)
         OR `constitutes distributing an intimate image after defences` (a's `sexual image`)
         OR `constitutes threatening to distribute an intimate image` (a's `sexual image`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes sexual exposure` IF
        `constitutes sexual exposure` (a's `sexual image`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a child abuse material offence` IF
        (   `constitutes using a child in producing child abuse material` (a's `sexual image`)
         OR `constitutes a child abuse material offence after defences` (a's `sexual image`)
         OR `constitutes exploitation by abusive material of a minor` (a's `sexual image`) (a's `sexual context`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
